<title>USA: Man Sang sees FY97 net of $5.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Man Sang sees FY97 net of $5.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Fla. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Man Sang Holdings Inc, a Hong Kong pearl supplier, said on Monday that it expected fiscal 1997 net income of $5.3 million, a 31 percent gain from the previous year, when it posted earnings of $4.1 million.</p>
<p>The company forecast fiscal 1997 sales of $35 million.</p>
<p>Based on the existing number of shares of outstanding common stock, the forecast earnings per share for fiscal year 1997 will be $1.41, the company said.</p>
